es. Therefore, B is more favorable in terms of skewness as defined. So, the reason would prefer B. Thus, the relevant information is: A has no favorable outcomes (all negative), B has 20% chance of 0 (a favorable outcome), so B has more probability on favorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason applies and can be used to compare the lotteries.",
